            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Both use the G2 one-watering formula, are rain-safe 15 minutes after activation and share the same coverage figures and residential warranty. Maxx G2 is rated for joints up to 4 inches, is approved over concrete slabs and comes in four colours. Supersand Bond G2 tops out at 2 inches, is not for slab overlays and comes in Beige and Slate Grey."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does Gator Maxx G2 take to cure before rain?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Alliance rates Gator Maxx G2 rain-safe 15 minutes after water activation on a traditional compacted base, and 24 hours on an overlay over concrete. It must be installed above 32 degrees Fahrenheit in dry conditions. Alliance's FAQ says you can walk or drive on it after 24 hours if it is dry."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a 50 lb bag of Gator Maxx G2 cover?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Alliance quotes 65 to 85 square feet on narrow joints of 1/8 to 3/8 inch and 22 to 42 square feet on wide joints of 3/4 to 1 1/4 inch, for pavers about 2 3/8 inches thick. Black Diamond is quoted slightly lower. Real coverage depends on joint uniformity, so buy an extra bag."
          }
